# Data conversion between gibibyte and kibibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gibibyte and kibibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GiB to 1048576KiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5GiB yields 1572864.0KiB; backward, converting 1KiB to 0.0000GiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KiB yields 0.0000GiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(forward_whole->to(KiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(forward_fractional->to(KiB))
backward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(backward_whole->to(GiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(backward_fractional->to(GiB))

<<< stdout
1048576KiB
1572864.0KiB
0.0000GiB
0.0000GiB

<<< stderr
